// RPC handler decisions from the fixed Python reference (`xeHentai/rpc.py`).
//
// Every business decision lives here: method lookup (the `xeH.` prefix and
// camelCase to snake_case mapping of `rpc.py:343-349`), the 13-method
// allowlist and private-name refusal (`rpc.py:350-353`), the updateConfig
// key filter and proxy no-op rule (`rpc.py:431-435`), the listTasks level
// selector (`rpc.py:437-450`), the getImage range quirk (`rpc.py:488-501`),
// per-method arity rules, and the public task/config field projections
// (`rpc.py:427-428`, `rpc.py:446-450`). Native Rust supplies the wire bytes,
// the exact-literal token check, the App mutations and the serialization of
// the values this module selects; it never decides a method, a default, a
// filter or a projection itself.
//
// Ownership note: the script borrow checker rejects slicing a local and
// then moving that same local. String predicates therefore run through tiny
// helpers on explicit copies (`has_prefix("" + name, ...)`), slices apply to
// parameters or helper-locals only, and every selected value is moved exactly
// once. The verbose nesting below follows the proven `rss/filters/match.rss`
// statement shapes.

// --- small character helpers -------------------------------------------
// The reference only folds an ASCII lower-to-upper boundary (`([a-z])([A-Z])`).
// These explicit arms keep exactly that behavior without a regex engine.

